## Rendered contract

- Awareness loop: `{{ awareness_loop_hz }} Hz`
- Self model: `{{ self_model }}`
- Memory consolidator: `{{ memory_consolidator }}`
- Dossier store: `{{ dossier_store }}`
- Engine ref: `74218cf762d7b704732b3a22ff1dd90e49273aee`

The entry point validates this overlay against `maistro-turing`'s
`TuringConfig` and emits a non-secret readiness document. It does not start an
unbounded autonomous loop or claim that an external model provider is
configured.

The defaults (`minimal`, consolidator `off`, filesystem dossier) minimize
autonomous processing and retained personal data. Enable broader behavior only
after documenting its policy and retention boundaries.

## Local verification

```bash
uv sync --extra dev
uv run pytest
uv run {{ project_slug }} --check
```

## Container verification

Build-time dependency installation is isolated in `Dockerfile`; the runtime
container does not install packages.

```bash
docker compose -f deploy/compose.yml build
docker compose -f deploy/compose.yml run --rm {{ project_slug }}
```

{% if dossier_store == 'obsidian' -%}
Set `OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH` to the host vault directory before invoking Compose.
The bind mount is read/write because the selected dossier adapter is intended
to persist updates; scope that directory to a dedicated vault.
{% else -%}
The default named volume stores dossier data under `/data/dossier`.
{% endif %}

## Governance

The ADR seed cites `maistro-engine#ADR-019`, `maistro-engine#ADR-032`, and
`maistro-engine#ADR-033`. Contract tests use both ADR-032 marker axes, and
`cosmic-ray.toml` follows the engine's bounded source-to-test mutation pattern.
